  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Just as the fortune teller predicted, identical twin bellboys summon Chef Barinov upstairs to room two-oh-seven, where Mikhail Dzhekovich has gambled away everything he owns.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Прошу прощения, здесь мой друг.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Витя, это правда ты пришёл?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты представляешь, я всё проиграл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Я проиграл всё, что у меня было.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Зачем я вообще с ним сел играть?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы его самого не выиграли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Жаль, тогда я его забираю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Настя, ты телефон дома забыла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо тебе большое, дорогой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Скажи мне правду, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Гости за столиком уже ждут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Иди быстрее прими у них заказ.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Прошу прощения, здесь мой друг.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excuse me, my friend is in here.' Notice how Russian expresses 'ask for' and 'friend' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Витя, это правда ты пришёл?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, is it really you who came?' The meaning hinges on 'this' working together with 'arrived' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Ты представляешь, я всё проиграл.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can you imagine, I lost everything.' Notice how Russian expresses 'you' and 'lost' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Я проиграл всё, что у меня было.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I lost everything that I had.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'I' before landing on 'was'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "mikhail",
      "t": "Зачем я вообще с ним сел играть?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why did I even sit down to play with him?' Notice how Russian expresses 'why' and 'to play' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы его самого не выиграли?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you not win him too?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'won'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Жаль, тогда я его забираю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Too bad, then I am taking him away.' In Russian, the idea of 'it is a pity' flows naturally into 'am taking' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Настя, ты телефон дома забыла.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Nastya, you forgot your phone at home.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Nastya' before landing on 'forgot'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Спасибо тебе большое, дорогой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you very much, my dear.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'thank you', while 'expensive' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kostya",
      "t": "Скажи мне правду, пожалуйста.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Tell me the truth, please.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'say' before landing on 'please'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Гости за столиком уже ждут.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The guests at the table are already waiting.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'guests' and 'for' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Иди быстрее прими у них заказ.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Go quickly and take their order.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'go' before landing on 'order'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
